Real-user price impact is the admin formula and nothing else:

* shared/price-from-imbalance: computeDeterministicPips / previewDeterministicPriceImpact
  are the single shared function behind the engine, the admin preview endpoint and the
  Live Trade Log. A formula move below one quote tick (0.00001 = 0.1 pip) now registers
  as exactly one tick in the trade's direction — flat, price-level independent.
* engine/market-state: the post-clamp directional nudge (enforceImmediateDirectionalMove,
  sized with the price-scaled pip) no longer runs for real trades; it stayed active after
  the deterministic path was introduced and moved small real orders by up to ~1 pip
  depending on book skew and price level, which the admin preview never showed. The
  replay applies the same rule so audit and live pricing agree. Each tick reports the
  realised move on the 5-decimal quote.
* settlement: the Price Movement Audit snapshot was taken with getPipImpactConfig() in the
  settlement-worker process, which never loads the live config, so every queued
  settlement stored the compiled-in defaults (log / 5 / 1) and a wrong expected end
  price. The engine leader now records the config the round really used (including a
  per-round override) when the round closes; settlement reads that record, falls back
  to the durable Redis config, and uses the configured freeze seconds.
* engine: admin saves are pushed on engine:events:market.sensitivity.v1 and applied
  immediately (pollers remain the fallback). New engine:events:trade.priced.v1 carries
  one attribution row per priced trade, never coalesced, so the Live Trade Log sees every
  trade; the API persists it independently of the price-tick persistence flag.
* api: GET /admin/market-sensitivity/preview (engine-exact preview with live price and
  effective sensitivity); live trade log totals measured on the price path (start → now)
  with real / NPC / other split, formula vs actual per real row, sensitivity in force;
  change-log search / field / date filters server-side; audit list returns every settled
  round with PASS/FAIL, window summary and the Market Sensitivity multiplier (the column
  used to show the round's event multiplier); replay expected end price keeps 5 decimals.

Tests: price-impact-deterministic.spec (8) — exact 16.0 pips for the reported $100k case,
price-level independence, round-state independence, quote-tick floor, curves, replay
parity; shared 219/222 and engine 82/95 (all remaining failures pre-existing, untouched);
workbench: NPC-off trades exact at every size, push applied before a trade 300 ms after
save, NPC-on log separating the exact real move from NPC ticks, settlement snapshot
correct, admin page checks 20/20.

